<title>UK: HSBC JamesCapel shuffles equity strategists.</title>
<headline>HSBC JamesCapel shuffles equity strategists.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC James Capel said on Wedesday it had hired Bill O'Neil as international investment strategist, after he completed an MSC in economics from the University of London.</p>
<p>O'Neill, who had previously worked for Capel in Australia, replaces Peter Oppenheimer who will become European strategist after three years in his previous role.</p>
<p>A new position of european quantitative strategist will be filled by Oliver Kamm, reflecting the aim of the company to increase the quantitative input to its strategic analysis.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
